      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town began as a company town founded by the Three States Lumber Company in the early 1900s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burdette%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1906, Three States completed a large sawmill in Burdette, fueling the local lumber boom.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Burdette%2C_Arkansas",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A 1907 railway, the Blytheville, Burdette and Mississippi River line, ran from Wolverton Landing to Blytheville, branching into Burdette.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
